WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.600
You've built a following.

2
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:02.800
Ten thousand people.

3
00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:04.400
Maybe a hundred thousand.

4
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:06.000
You post every day.

5
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.600
The likes roll in.

6
00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:11.200
But here's the hard truth — you don't own

7
00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:12.400
any of it.

8
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:14.800
Today we're talking about the difference

9
00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:17.600
between being a creator and being a

10
00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:18.000
builder.

11
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.200
And why one path gives you real power,

12
00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:23.600
while the other keeps you renting.

13
00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:24.800
Let's define terms.

14
00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:27.600
A creator makes content on platforms they

15
00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:28.400
don't control.

16
00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:28.800
Instagram.

17
00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:29.200
TikTok.

18
00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:29.600
YouTube.

19
00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:31.200
You're creating value, yes.

20
00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:33.600
But the platform owns the relationship

21
00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:34.800
with your audience.

22
00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:36.800
They decide what gets shown.

23
00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:38.400
They change the algorithm.

24
00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:40.400
They can ban you tomorrow.

25
00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:42.800
You're renting space in someone else's

26
00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:43.200
house.

27
00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:44.400
And the rent?

28
00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:47.200
It's your time, your energy, your ideas.

29
00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:48.800
Now meet the builder.

30
00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:51.200
A builder creates things they own.

31
00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:52.000
A website.

32
00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:52.800
An app.

33
00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:53.600
A tool.

34
00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:54.400
A product.

35
00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:57.200
When someone uses what you built, they

36
00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:58.800
come directly to you.

37
00:00:58.800 --> 00:00:59.600
No middleman.

38
00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:02.400
No algorithm deciding if your work is

39
00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:03.200
worthy today.

40
00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:04.800
You control the experience.

41
00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:06.400
You control the relationship.

42
00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:08.000
You own the asset.

43
00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.600
And here's the kicker — what you build can

44
00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:14.000
work for you while you sleep.

45
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:15.200
Let's get concrete.

46
00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:17.600
You're a fitness creator with fifty

47
00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:18.800
thousand Instagram followers.

48
00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:19.200
Impressive.

49
00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:21.200
But Instagram changes the algorithm.

50
00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:23.600
Your reach drops eighty percent overnight.

51
00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:24.800
Your income vanishes.

52
00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:26.800
Now imagine you're a builder.

53
00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:28.800
You have a fitness app.

54
00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:30.400
Five thousand paying users.

55
00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:32.000
Instagram could disappear tomorrow.

56
00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:33.600
Your business keeps running.

57
00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:34.800
That's the difference.

58
00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:36.000
One is fragile.

59
00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:37.600
The other is antifragile.

60
00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:39.600
Here's what most people miss.

61
00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:42.000
Being a builder doesn't mean abandoning

62
00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:42.800
content creation.

63
00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:44.000
The smartest move?

64
00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:44.800
Be both.

65
00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:46.800
Use platforms to reach people.

66
00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:49.600
But drive them to something you own.

67
00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:50.400
Your website.

68
00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:51.600
Your email list.

69
00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:52.400
Your app.

70
00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:53.600
Platforms are megaphones.

71
00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:54.400
Use them.

72
00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:56.800
But never make them your foundation.

73
00:01:56.800 --> 00:01:58.800
Build on land you own.

74
00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:02.000
Why does this matter for you right now?

75
00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:04.800
Because you're about to learn to code.

76
00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:07.600
And coding is the ultimate builder skill.

77
00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:10.400
It lets you create things that exist

78
00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:12.000
independent of any platform.

79
00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:13.600
A website that's yours.

80
00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:16.400
A tool that solves a real problem.

81
00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:18.000
An asset that compounds.

82
00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:21.600
You're not learning to code to get a job.

83
00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:24.800
You're learning to code to own your work.

84
00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:26.400
So here's your exercise.

85
00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:29.600
List one thing you currently rent — a

86
00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:31.600
platform where you're building an

87
00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:32.000
audience.

88
00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:35.200
Then list one thing you could own instead.

89
00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:37.200
Maybe it's a simple website.

90
00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:39.200
Maybe it's an email list.

91
00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:42.000
Maybe it's a tool you wish existed.

92
00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:43.200
Don't overthink it.

93
00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:44.800
Just write it down.

94
00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:47.200
Next lesson, we're diving into the

95
00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:50.400
Nabulines method — how we're going to turn

96
00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:53.200
you from creator into builder in the

97
00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:54.400
fastest way possible.

98
00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:55.600
See you there.
